{"title":"2005 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 12B Problems\">2005 AMC 12B #6</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems\">2005 AMC 10B #10</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Trig)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Trig)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Stewart&#39;s_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Stewart's Theorem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/6/2f63fb1414ca54984fbd96cadc0c501d2a96fc8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=BC=7$\" width=\"114\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/2/d5204a6910d20a4ff2968ad55671e3cfa350e9da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=2$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is a point on line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> lies between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/d/57ddc2c20d3d3c273905e78f11f0e4b44d2524e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=8$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/b/20bf9f8b743fba6a44120a8b1c3eef4f8f0570b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\ 3      \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }\\ 2\\sqrt{3}      \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }\\ 4      \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }\\ 5      \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\ 4\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"431\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Draw height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/e/20e8e26d580012b86d8fe55e70e5740908c35af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CH$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> (Perpendicular line from point C to line AD). We have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/0/e40ff3d5b2a162027d2b561410e3d2565ed74a5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BH=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" />. By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/7/46751b24a5eeee3a1c49c7752786377ec36602b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CH=\\sqrt{48}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/d/57ddc2c20d3d3c273905e78f11f0e4b44d2524e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=8$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/f/b7f216e139f86c04ee78a9da44c137effef8b83c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HD=\\sqrt{8^2-48}=\\sqrt{16}=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"219\" height=\"19\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/6/366228eb4d09a0cae16f087c28a7e11a9d8e98b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=HD-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"117\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/d/7edfc5c2830382d6203133decbb06151697c01ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"112\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Trig.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Trig)\">Solution 2 (Trig)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Trig)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>After drawing out a diagram, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/6/7265016fd6ded0e7e44e56df8f0846bc65b15f49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{ABC}=\\theta$\" width=\"88\" height=\"13\" />. By the Law of Cosines, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/4/8d4a5993c19a09e720bee1224d620e009cd39e3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7^2=2^2+7^2-2(7)(2)\\cos{\\theta} \\rightarrow 0=4-28\\cos{\\theta} \\rightarrow \\cos{\\theta}=\\frac{1}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"464\" height=\"37\" />. In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/86644a0d74ba9ba18fc2e69713901863ab6c3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CBD$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/d/0dd7f316a5e1c1d366823f48f03d6e62ec991066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CBD}=(180-\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"18\" />, and using the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e30f93c838ec96a017d306466686bac21aac74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(180-\\theta)=-\\cos{\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"174\" height=\"18\" /> and Law of Cosines one more time: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/1/d014d18b5745b9c24afc619a5ef2a4c4a9b8668a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8^2=7^2+x^2-2(7)(x)\\left( \\frac{-1}{7} \\right) \\rightarrow 64=49+x^2+2x \\rightarrow x^2+2x-15=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"564\" height=\"43\" />. The only positive value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which gives the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />. Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/b/26b24dfda9c973a310d9a971b5ec21834e73f10d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~Bowser498\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Stewart.27s_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Stewart's_Theorem)\">Solution 3 (Stewart's Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Stewart&#39;s Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/3/1436a084ce37d9e6adb20ccc39fb9c68d8f8a9ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=k$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" />. Then, by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Stewart%27s_Theorem\" title=\"Stewart&#39;s Theorem\">Stewart's Theorem</a>, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/a/59a5971ac7446f62aa2e71f3c0921bd0e97c32fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k(2+k)+7^2(2+k)=7^2k+8^2\\cdot 2 \\implies k^2+2k-15=0 \\implies k=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"604\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~apsid\n</p><p>~edited by always90degrees (tiny fix, sign error)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B\">2005 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_1